## Why This Is Asked

Real-time network paths require precise tail latency insight without burdening performance. eBPF offers low-overhead, per-event visibility ideal for diagnosing bursts in UDP data paths.

## Key Concepts

- eBPF tracing (bpftrace/bpfcc) for live latency data
- Tracepoints vs kprobes for kernel events
- Per-CPU histograms and BPF maps for aggregation
- Data-path isolation with tc and minimal instrumentation
- Safe rollback/guardrails if overhead grows

## Code Example

```javascript
function percentile(arr, p){
  if (!arr.length) return 0;
  const sorted = [...arr].sort((a,b)=>a-b);
  const idx = Math.ceil((sorted.length-1)*p/100);
  return sorted[idx];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt this plan if TLS/DTLS terminates before the RX path?
- What thresholds and sampling rates would you choose for a fleet of hosts, and how would you automate rollback across them?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests Linux networking, virtualization concepts, and QoS under multi-tenant load in a real-world VPN gateway.

## Key Concepts

- Per-tenant namespaces/VRF routing
- XDP/BPF for ACLs and QoS
- tc/qdisc HTB or fq_codel per tenant
- IRQ affinity and CPU pinning
- NUMA awareness and tenant cgroups
- Observability with iperf/netperf

## Code Example

```javascript
// High-level pseudo steps (not executed as-is)
const tenants = ["t1","t2"];
for (const t of tenants) {
  const ns = createNamespace(`vn_${t}`);
  setupVRF(ns, t);
  bindVpnWorkerToNamespace(ns);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would tail latency be measured and bounded at 99th percentile?
- How to safely onboard/offboard tenants without disruption?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests ability to design advanced observability with safe overhead, tenant isolation, and rollback.

## Key Concepts
- eBPF tracepoints, container lifecycle, per-tenant tagging, tail-latency analysis, rollout and rollback.

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo-eBPF sketch: tag events with tenant and record startup latency
tracepoint("container_start", (ctx) => {
  const tenant = getCurrentTenantId();
  recordLatency(tenant, now() - startTime);
});
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you validate that tracing does not perturb startup times under load?
- What metrics and dashboards would you expose to operators?
